.build/
.swiftpm/
.DS_Store

# Build artifacts from running the CI build commands locally: the workflow uses
# relative `-clonedSourcePackagesDirPath SourcePackages` / `-derivedDataPath
# DerivedData.noindex`, so a local repro drops these in the repo root.
#
# That relative path is also why the derived-data root carries a `.noindex`
# suffix: a local reproduction of a documented command builds a real application
# bundle inside the checkout, and every bundle sitting in an indexed directory is
# surfaced system-wide as an installed application. A directory whose name ends
# in `.noindex` is skipped by the metadata importer wherever it lives, which is
# the one name-level opt-out available here — so the suffix belongs to the
# *name*, not to any one command. Pinned by `ReleaseWorkflowTests`.
SourcePackages/
DerivedData.noindex/

# The pre-rename name, kept as a legacy guard rather than deleted. Nothing
# writes here any more — the workflows and every documented command name the
# `.noindex` root above, and `ReleaseWorkflowTests` pins that. What this entry
# defends is the *other* direction: every clone that ever ran the old commands
# still holds this directory on disk, and renaming the entry instead of adding
# beside it un-ignores gigabytes of stale build output the moment the rename
# lands. That is not hypothetical — it committed 22 816 files here once.
DerivedData/

# The release archive path, used verbatim by `.github/workflows/release.yml`,
# `docs/RELEASING.md` and the archive command in `CLAUDE.md`
# (`-archivePath build.noindex/Pisaka-macOS.xcarchive`), plus the zip staging
# directory beside it. A local release repro must leave `git status` clean: the
# build number is passed on the command line and never committed, so the archive
# it produces must not be the thing that dirties the tree instead.
#
# The `.noindex` suffix is here for the same reason it is on the derived-data
# root above: an archive holds the application bundle itself, reproduced
# verbatim in the checkout root, and a name ending in `.noindex` is the only way
# to keep the metadata importer out of it by name alone. Pinned by
# `ReleaseWorkflowTests`.
build.noindex/

# The pre-rename name, kept as a legacy guard for the same reason `DerivedData/`
# is above: a checkout that archived before the rename still holds this
# directory, and this entry is what keeps a stale copy of it out of a commit.
build/

# The one-time Sparkle key ceremony and the tooling it needs, all of which
# `docs/RELEASING.md` runs from a checkout. `generate_keys -x` writes the EdDSA
# **private** half to a file, and that half leaking is unrecoverable for every
# copy already installed — they verify updates against the public half baked
# into their own bundle. The doc exports it outside the tree; this is the second
# guard, so that a `git add -A` between exporting and deleting it cannot commit
# a private key into history. The pattern is a glob rather than a bare
# `private-key.txt` on purpose: gitignore matches a name-only pattern against the
# whole basename, so `private-key.txt` would not cover
# `pisaka-sparkle-private-key.txt` — the exact filename `docs/RELEASING.md` tells
# you to export to. A guard that misses the documented name is no guard at all.
# The tools directory, the tarball and a locally generated feed are the rest of
# that ceremony's untracked debris.
*private-key*.txt
sparkle-tools/
Sparkle-*.tar.xz
/appcast.xml

# The Xcode project is generated by XcodeGen from `project.yml` — do not commit
# the project itself. But DO commit the resolved Swift Package pins it produces,
# so transitive dependency versions (e.g. tree-sitter, swift-argument-parser)
# stay locked for reproducible builds — the role the root `Package.resolved`
# played before the app target moved into the Xcode project. (Git can only
# re-include a file when no parent directory is excluded, so each level is
# excluded with `/*` and the next path component re-included in turn — which is
# why the whole `Pisaka.xcodeproj` directory is not excluded outright.)
Pisaka.xcodeproj/*
!Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace
Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/*
!Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata
Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/*
!Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm
Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/*
!Pisaka.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/swiftpm/Package.resolved
